Bandit Level 11 - Level 12

Challenge: Decode the ROT13-encoded password stored in data.txt.

Solution:

cat data.txt | tr 'A-Za-z' 'N-ZA-Mn-za-m'

Explanation:
cat data.txt displays the contents of the file.
tr 'A-Za-z' 'N-ZA-Mn-za-m' applies the ROT13 cipher by shifting each uppercase and lowercase letter 13 positions.

Password: GROozWPO8QyN0mGrjUkID0WCYkZiQxrN

What I learned:
tr replaces characters position by position. 
For ROT13, A-Z maps to N-ZA-M and a-z maps to n-za-m, shifting every letter by 13 places.
